    "image_text_cta_g3W7Qt": {
      "type": "image-text-cta",
      "disabled": true,
      "custom_css": [
        "img {aspect-ratio: 1/1;}"
      ],
      "name": "Image with Text CTA",
      "settings": {
        "subheading": "",
        "heading": "How Are Lab-Grown Diamonds Created?",
        "heading_size": "h1",
        "text": "<p>Lab-grown diamonds are created by recreating the environment needed for diamond formation. A small diamond seed is placed inside a controlled chamber where carbon atoms gradually form into a diamond crystal.</p><p>There are two primary methods used today:</p><h3>Chemical Vapour Deposition (CVD)</h3><p>CVD technology grows diamonds by placing a diamond seed inside a chamber filled with carbon-rich gases. Under controlled conditions, carbon atoms attach layer by layer, creating a diamond crystal.</p><h3>High Pressure High Temperature (HPHT)</h3><p>HPHT technology recreates the extreme pressure and temperature conditions found deep inside the Earth. This process transforms carbon material into a diamond crystal.</p>",
        "color_scheme": "",
        "full_width": true,
        "button_label_1": "",
        "button_link_1": "#",
        "button_style_1": "secondary",
        "button_label_2": "",
        "button_link_2": "#",
        "button_style_2": "primary",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/page_1_image_2.png",
        "image_ratio": "landscape",
        "layout_desktop": "image-left",
        "layout_mobile": "image-first",
        "margin_top": "no-indent",
        "margin_bottom": "no-indent"
      }
